<meta type=article title="Callout types">
</meta>

<section | Admonitions>

The five admonition types render with distinct per-type callout styling
(accent border, background tint, and a CSS icon); the generic `sidebar`
type keeps the plain boxed look.

<aside type=note title="A note" | Plain informational note.>

<aside type=warning | Do not run this on production data.>

<aside type=tip title="Reproducibility" | Use a fixed random seed for every run.>

<aside type=info | Background context the reader may want.>

<aside type=caution | This step is destructive and cannot be undone.>

<aside type=sidebar | A plain sidebar — no admonition styling, just the box.>

<section | Numbered box>

A numbered aside joins the "Box" series and carries a title above and a
caption below.

<aside #box:setup +numbered type=note title="Experimental setup" caption="The full calibration rig." |
The apparatus is calibrated before each run.
>
